141
00:14:31,420 --> 00:14:37,220
Hello everybody. It is my honor to introduce our respectable speaker for today's

142
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:39,240
lecture, Dr. Thomas Wood.

143
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:45,720
Dr. Wood has written numerous articles and books on the topic of communication and

144
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,280
how to communicate effectively.

145
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:49,860
Welcome, Dr. Wood.

146
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,320
Good morning, everyone.

147
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:54,460
I'm very glad to have a lecture with you.

148
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:58,380
Today I'd like to talk about how to communicate effectively.

149
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:04,280
Effective communication is an essential component of human relationships, whether in

150
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:09,600
the workplace, at school, among friends, between couples, or within a household.

151
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:15,460
Highly functional, successful family groups tend to be those that communicate

152
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:20,560
effectively, while the lack of such communication is frequently found in troubled

153
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:23,540
families, according to a research company.

154
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:29,060
Learning and practicing effective communication techniques is well worth the time

155
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:34,840
and effort, resulting in stronger interpersonal ties and greater familial

156
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:37,940
satisfaction. My tips are as follows.

157
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,620
Think first, speak later.

158
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:45,920
Few people would stand before an audience or class and present a speech without

159
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:47,380
advanced preparation.

160
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:53,260
Gathering thoughts, ideas, and information are critical for communicating in an

161
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:55,380
organized and effective way.

162
00:15:55,940 --> 00:16:01,480
Setting priorities can be helpful, especially when preparing to discuss a complex

163
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:07,860
issue. Furthermore, stepping away from a problem before discussing it allows time to

164
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:13,780
gain objectivity, as well as empathy for the other person or persons involved.

165
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,200
Be fully present.

166
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:20,740
Effective communication is possible only in the present moment.

167
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:26,620
Bringing past conflicts into the current discussion serves only to heighten negative

168
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:30,220
emotions and be bad for a productive conversation.

169
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:35,540
A sharp focus on the topic at hand is essential for clear and effective

170
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:41,600
communication, and it is also helpful to keep outside distractions to a minimum.

171
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:49,400
Text messages, phone calls, and emails can all wait until a later time, and worries

172
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:54,660
about work, school, or other issues can be put on hold as well.

173
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,420
Use nonverbal cues.

174
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:04,100
Nonverbal cues, such as facial expressions, body language, and hand gestures, play

175
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:06,640
an important role in effective communication.

176
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:13,160
Just as a badly chosen word or a raised voice can upset a listener and close the

177
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:19,380
door to further dialogue, so too can an unintentionally aggressive nonverbal cue.

178
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:26,140
One way to ensure that nonverbal signals don't undermine verbal communication is to

179
00:17:26,140 --> 00:17:31,000
remain calm and avoid becoming overly stressed during a discussion.

180
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:36,600
Staying calm and maintaining a comfortable amount of eye contact while respecting

181
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:40,360
personal space can increase receptivity.

182
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:46,880
Listen actively. Effective communication includes the ability to listen well.

183
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:53,200
In addition to avoiding obvious distractions, such as cell phones and using body

184
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:58,720
language to demonstrate attentiveness, it is also important to allow the other

185
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:03,840
person to finish speaking before formulating our own response.

186
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:09,460
Paraphrasing what the other person has said to make sure we have understood

187
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:15,540
correctly and refraining from offering advice unless asked to do so are two more

188
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:17,300
ways to listen effectively.

189
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:19,860
Thank you for your listening.

190
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:24,460
Hope this lecture will be helpful and you will be a better communicator.

